{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:26e1e3aaab6dcab8","name":"Lluma","source":{"id":"source:reference-26e1e3aaab6dcab8","title":"Lluma","revision":21206,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:21:19Z","sha256":"c22b747ca470861f2e5f133149710ea70aed17e6f94866ac4e75f6613a38e714","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21206","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Lluma&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-26e1e3aaab6dcab8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["This large amphibian is covered in a slimy gray-brown hide. Two lines of green bioluminescent spots, which start just behind its bulbous eyes, pulse along either side of its prominent backbone. It possesses a long, curving neck, four long knobby legs that end in four-toed feet, and a short, stubby tail."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Lluma are a large, long-limbed species that roam the surface of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"}," in herds. They are herbivorous, grazing on a wide variety of fungi as they roam. Lluma herds typically consist of at least twenty individuals, although as many as two hundred travel Nyriaan's equatorial regions in larger herds. The creatures are considered a delicious staple of the local menu, and some of the smaller herds have been hunted to death by colonists and settlers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Lluma are hermaphroditic and are able to assume one of three genders depending on the composition of the herd and the season. A single bull usually protects the herd, although large herds can have several. Fertile females, also known as cows, make up about twenty percent of any given herd. They mate continually with the bull, storing fertilized eggs in large pouches until the young hatch. The remaining eighty percent of the herd maintain a neutral gender, neither male nor female. The purpose of these neuters is not completely clear, but they seem to perform a protective role by surrounding fertile males and females as the herd travels.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Biologists study Lluma because the species seems to have an innate reliance on the violent tempests that wrack the planetary surface. Lluma herds follow in the paths of prior tempests, sometimes changing direction when their route intersects the path of another tempest. Scientists hope that research into this behavior yields clues that might help to predict future tempests.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Tactics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Lluma prefer to flee rather than fight, although Lluma bulls protect their herds violently if provoked. Cows can also become violent when their young are endangered. In either case, Lluma of any gender charge and trample enemies, crushing them until they exhibit no sign of life.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Lluma Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +11\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href"